     <a class="skip-link" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a>

     <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
       <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
         <div class="eyebrow">Cat FAQ</div>
         <h1 id="page-title">Answers to common cat questions</h1>
         <p class="lead">
           A calm, readable FAQ for curious humans and their very opinionated companions.
           Tap a question to expand the answer.
         </p>
       </section>

       <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" id="q1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a1">
               Why do cats purr?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="a1" aria-labelledby="q1">
             <p>
               Cats purr to express comfort, but they also use it to self-soothe, communicate,
               and sometimes to help them stay calm when they are stressed or hurt.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" id="q2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a2">
               Do cats need a lot of playtime?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="a2" aria-labelledby="q2">
             <p>
               Yes. Short, regular play sessions help cats burn energy, sharpen hunting instincts,
               and avoid boredom. Two or three focused sessions a day is a great start.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" id="q3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a3">
               Why do cats knead blankets?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="a3" aria-labelledby="q3">
             <p>
               Kneading is a comforting behavior linked to kittenhood. Adult cats often knead when
               they feel safe, relaxed, or especially attached to their favorite human.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" id="q4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a4">
               What does a cat's tail mean?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="a4" aria-labelledby="q4">
             <p>
               A cat's tail is a useful mood meter. A tall tail often signals confidence, a swishing
               tail can mean irritation, and a puffed tail usually means the cat is startled.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2 class="question">
             <button type="button" id="q5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a5">
               How can I make a cat-friendly home?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="a5" aria-labelledby="q5">
             <p>
               Offer vertical spaces, scratching posts, fresh water, clean litter boxes, and quiet
               places to rest. Cats also appreciate predictable routines and a few cozy hiding spots.
             </p>
             <ul>
               <li>Keep food and litter areas separate.</li>
               <li>Use toys that encourage stalking and pouncing.</li>
               <li>Let the cat choose when to cuddle.</li>
             </ul>
           </div>
         </div>
       </section>
     </main>

     <script>
       const disclosures = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

       disclosures.forEach((item) => {
         const trigger = item.querySelector("button[aria-expanded]");
         const panel = item.querySelector(".details");

         trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
         panel.hidden = true;

         const setOpen = (open) => {
           trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open));
           panel.hidden = !open;
         };

         trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
           setOpen(trigger.getAttribute("aria-expanded") !== "true");
         });

         trigger.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
           if (event.key === "Escape" && trigger.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
             setOpen(false);
             trigger.focus();
           }
         });
       });
     </script>
   </body>
 </html>

